  "result": "Excellent! All 65 tests pass. Here's what I created:\n\n**src/numbering.js** \u2014 `nextInvoiceNumber(existingNumbers, issueDate)`:\n- Extracts the year from the issueDate (YYYY-MM-DD format)\n- Finds the highest counter used in that year\n- Returns the next invoice number with format `INV-<year>-<counter>`\n- Counter is 4 digits, zero-padded (0001, 0002, ..., 9999)\n- Resets to 0001 for each new year\n- Gracefully ignores malformed numbers\n\n**issueInvoice(invoice, existingNumbers)** in src/invoices.js:\n- Validates invoice is in draft status (returns `fail('NOT_DRAFT')` otherwise)\n- Assigns the next available invoice number via `nextInvoiceNumber`\n- Changes status from 'draft' to 'issued'\n- Returns `ok(newInvoice)` preserving all other data\n- Never mutates the original invoice\n\n**Tests** \u2014 17 new test cases:\n- 10 for numbering: empty lists, increments, year restarts, malformed data, mixed years, any order\n- 7 for issuing: basic flow, existing numbers, different years, non-draft rejection, immutability",
